# libFuzzer dictionary for the url client response-side harness - status lines, chunk framing, SSE
# fields and header syntax. Tokens are shared across all four oracles; each build only reaches the
# ones its own grammar can use, and libFuzzer ignores the rest.
#
# Control bytes are hex-escaped (\x0d\x0a, not \r\n) - libFuzzer's dictionary reader does not accept
# a bare backslash-r/backslash-n escape (see r.dict's "\x0a" for the same convention).
"HTTP/1.0 "
"HTTP/1.1 "
"\x0d\x0a"
"\x0d\x0a\x0d\x0a"
"Content-Length: "
"Transfer-Encoding: chunked"
"Connection: close"
"Location: "
"Set-Cookie: "
"Last-Event-ID: "
";"
"data: "
"event: "
"id: "
": "
"\x0a\x0a"
"0\x0d\x0a\x0d\x0a"
